SRC/hc_utils -- one change made for this collection===================================================compress.c (2026-09-15).  Six lines after #include <stdio.h>, inside#ifdef OSK, redefine putchar as fputc.  Microware's putchar macro evaluatesits argument twice when stdout is line-buffered -- a pipe or a terminal --so putchar(*bp++) when compressing and putchar(*--stackp) whenuncompressing skipped bytes there, and the output was corrupt.  Written toa file the macro evaluates it once, which is why it was always rightthere.  It still writes exactly those bytes: compressing SYS/termcap givesthe same 631 bytes, md5 c3694c4f0abc8ed599498e027b44945b, as before.CMDS/REBUILT/compress_rebuilt is this build.  CMDS/compress is the periodbinary; it writes the same bytes to a file, and corrupts a pipe the sameway the unchanged source did.